bibliograph (0.3.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bookhive catalog ISBNs are imported. `buzz.bookhive.catalogBook` carries
    `identifiers.isbn10`/`isbn13` on 82% of its records, and the edition
    mapping dropped them; they now reach `editions.identifiers` (ISBN-13
    first). `scripts/backfill-bookhive-isbns.ts` copies them onto the bh.*
    editions imported before the mapping changed, recomputing the CID, so the
    search scan no longer burns upstream calls on rows whose ISBN was already
    on-protocol.
  * `edition_work_backfill` remembers which editions the works backfill asked
    OpenLibrary about and found no match for, so a re-run skips them instead of
    spending another day re-asking the same questions: the second pass over 35
    editions took 92 ms against 10 s. `--retry-unmatched` ignores the markers
    when the upstream catalog has grown, and a successful link deletes the
    marker so an unlink is retried.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 11:33:19 -0500

bibliograph (0.3.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The daily ISBN backfill scans 83,000 rows per tick instead of 200, and its
    start timeout grows to one hour to cover the sequential enqueue, so the
    ~165k missing-ISBN backlog clears in about two days.

  * The works backfill no longer fabricates a work when OpenLibrary has no
    match: an unmatched edition is left with `work_uri` NULL instead of gaining
    a subjectless, contributor-less work row, and the summary reports those as
    `unmatched` rather than counting them as created. The scan also takes
    `--shard=<index>/<count>` (or SHARD_INDEX/SHARD_COUNT), so a 240k-edition
    catalog can be walked by several processes over disjoint uri slices.
  * A failed OpenLibrary search is now reported as `degraded` instead of an
    empty result, so the backfill defers those rows (and stops after 25 in a
    row) rather than recording "the catalog does not know this work" for a
    lookup that never happened — the breaker-open case that made an outage look
    like a catalog fact.
 
 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 11:05:52 -0500

bibliograph (0.3.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ISBN backfill tier 2 now writes the single search candidate it prunes to
    instead of only recording it: editions missing an ISBN gain one from the
    OpenLibrary/Google Books search, with the record CID recomputed. Rows the
    old shadow mode stamped are re-enqueued by the new
    scripts/enqueue-shadow-isbns.ts, the scan skips editions that already have
    a queued job, and the daily timer replaces the quarter-hour one.
  * Add the For You recommendation feed: catalog editions sharing subjects
    with the works a reader is reading and has read, excluding what they have
    shelved, backed by a partial index on editions.work_uri.

